  "description": "<h2>Event Details</h2>📍 <em>NEON at Battersea Power Station</em><br> <br> Featuring the pharaoh’s own coffin, royal treasures, and immersive galleries that transport visitors more than 3,000 years into the past, this exhibition arrives at Neon at Battersea Power Station in London following acclaimed runs in Paris, San Francisco, Sydney, and Tokyo.<br><ul><li>📆 Now open, with booking dates available until end of October.</li><li><br></li><li>Direct from the Egyptian Museum Cairo, 180 priceless treasures, each one over 3,000 years old. In the UK for the first and only time!</li></ul> <br>More influential than Tutankhamun, though far less mythologised, King Ramses II, widely known as Ramses the Great, ruled Egypt for nearly 67 years. 3,000 years later and he still remains one of history’s most iconic pharaohs.<br>&nbsp;<br> <img src=\"https://images.feverup.com/plan/photo/1045d800-4e18-11f1-9413-e2740a5cd1f2.jpg\" alt=\"180 Original Artefacts\"><strong>180 Original Artefacts</strong><br><br>Explore 180 original treasures over 3000 years old direct from Egyptian Museum, Cairo. Discover gold masks and silver coffins, beautifully preserved animal mummies and amulets, dazzling jewellery, and so much more.<br> <img src=\"https://images.feverup.com/plan/photo/cd806514-591e-11f1-920d-9608052fe954.jpg\" alt=\"Witness the Great King\"><strong>Witness the Great King</strong><br><br>Come face to face with the coffin of Ramses II, a work of inestimable value depicting the king as Osiris, god of the afterlife. More influential than Tutankhamun, Ramses the Great ruled for nearly 67 years and remains one of history’s most iconic pharaohs 3,000 years later.<br> <img src=\"https://images.feverup.com/plan/photo/105a52ee-4e18-11f1-9413-e2740a5cd1f2.jpg\" alt=\"Step Into History\"><strong>Step Into History</strong><br><br>Step into the world of Ramses the Great and journey through Egypt’s golden age, from the temples of Abu Simbel to the Valley of the Kings.<br> <img src=\"https://images.feverup.com/plan/photo/6851bb08-7ad8-11f1-8ee2-06fcf4c62e04.jpg\" alt=\"2+ Million Global Visitors\"><strong>Horrible Histories is taking over the museum&nbsp;</strong><br><br>Horrible Histories has joined forces with Ramses and the Pharaohs' Gold: The Exhibition, to present a hugely fun tour of the Awesome Egyptians! Take a terrible tour of priceless Egyptian artefacts with the great Ramses himself!<br>  &nbsp;<br><h2>General Information</h2>📅 Dates and times: select your date &amp; time directly in the ticket selector<br> 📌 Please see the experience FAQs <a href=\"https://ramsestheexhibition.co.uk/london/#faqs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a><br> ⭐ Horrible Histories has taken over the museum with hilarious family tours! Find tickets and more information <a href=\"https://feverup.com/m/674436\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a><br> 👤 Age requirement: recommended age is 5+<br> 📕 Up to 25% off for students - discount already applied to ticket<br> ♿ Accessibility: the venue is wheelchair accessible<br> 🎒 Please note that bags larger than A4 size are not permitted inside the venue. Any bags that are permitted must be worn on the front of the body<br> 🎧 Enhance your visit with an optional audio guide (available in six languages), narrated by historian, broadcaster, and author Dan Snow. Please bring your own headphones as headphones will not be provided on-site<br> 📩&nbsp;For Carer tickets, please contact Fever <a href=\"https://support.feverup.com/hc/en-us/requests/new\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a><br>  🎁 Gift memories to someone special! Purchase a gift card for Ramses and the Pharaohs' Gold: The Exhibition <a href=\"https://feverup.com/m/532621\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a><br> <br> <em>This exhibition is produced by Victory Hill Exhibitions Ltd (part of NEON Group) in partnership with the Egypt’s Supreme Council of Antiques and the Egyptian Museum.</em><br>",
